{
  "scope": "18 sequential fresh Linux processes; three repetitions rotate six worker/population combinations. One or four server workers on CPUs0-3, fixed four-thread client on CPUs4-7. Six measured seconds with one private pair, eight exact self-message/Close/EOF reconnect workers, zero idle rooms and either0/64/512 stable broadcast readers. Broadcast uses64 distinct1KiB templates/window16; every sender/body/FIFO checked, complete reader/message matrix, controlled exact departure notifications, independent counters/bytes/resources and client/server zero exits at gates. Client and server CPU sampled independently. No builds/profiles/other loads overlap ordinary cases. No before/after runtime optimization is being claimed.",
